# legs/adult/loco/tips: shoe tips under a long hem (A3's woman): drawn over the hem's under-edge
# The slice (P2b wave 1, FOLK-BODY); A3's pixels are the reference (docs/ref/style_a3). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# ROLLOUT ADULT-RIG (2026-10-22): every side walk and run view draws on layer belt, over the man's long hangs (robe, gown,
# kaftan, wrap at z 10 in hangFront), as the woman's hems already let it: the feet are std's shipped puts unchanged (heel
# and toe registered), so the planted shoe and the trailing toe show their rows and in the flight both boots peek under the
# raised hem: no floating bell (B11 wear T1 / T2). Idle, D / U and every other view as before.
# THE SIDE RUN, PROTO6 i2 (2026-10-22): the push's tips follow std's i2 push (the support's K3 toe at u -2); the swing
# boot is lifted inside a long hem, so only the support's toe shows (as the walk's passes).
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTO3 i1 (2026-10-21; std.pxm's header says how): the tips follow std's proto3 feet.
# THE SIDE RUN, PROTO2 i3 (2026-10-21; std.pxm's header says how): the run's tips follow std's i3 feet.
# History, superseded by proto2 i3 above:
# THE SIDE RUN, PROTO2 i2 (2026-10-21; std.pxm's header says how): the run's tips follow std's i2 feet (the landing boot
# whole, the push-off toe, a lifted swing boot's toe while its lift is in tipmax).
# History, superseded by proto2 i2 above:
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTO2 i1 (2026-10-21; std.pxm's header says how): the tips follow std's proto2 feet (a flat or
# heel-strike boot whole, a heel-off boot its ball end, a lifted toe-down boot its toe, a toe-up boot whole); under a long
# hem the walk's passes show the planted shoe only, in the near value (the swing shoe is lifted inside the hem), so the two
# passes are one drawing and the atlas keeps one (B10 LOCO).
# History, superseded by proto2 i1 above:
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTOTYPE i3 (2026-10-21; std.pxm's header says how): the tips follow std.pxm's i3 feet the i2
# way (a flat or heel-strike boot whole, a heel-off boot its ball end, a lifted toe-down boot its toe, a toe-up boot whole).
# History, superseded by prototype i3 above: prototype i2 (2026-10-21):
# (i2) THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTOTYPE i2 (2026-10-21; std.pxm's header says how): each side walk / run tip is the boot of
# std.pxm's key at the same placement, windowed to what shows under a long hem: a flat or heel-strike boot whole, a heel-off
# boot its ball end, a lifted toe-down boot its toe (cols 4-6), K3 its toe, the flight's toe-up boot whole.
# History, superseded by prototype i2 above: prototype i1 (2026-10-21):
# (i1) THE SIDE WALK AND RUN, PROTOTYPE i1 (2026-10-21; docs/ref/motion/RESEARCH.md; std.pxm's header says how): each side walk /
# run tip is the boot of std.pxm's key at the same placement, windowed to what shows under a long hem: a flat or heel-strike
# boot whole, a heel-off boot its ball end (the second put), a lifted toe-down boot its toe (cols 4-6), K3 its toe (cols 3-5
# lifted), K1 whole (the run flight's toe-up). Placed by `put` (pxc expands the stamps; `tags boots-stamped`).
# The motion rebuild's tips (superseded): each side walk / run tip was the boot of std.pxm's key at the same placement, 
#   (MOTION_P2 7.4) windowed to the stamp's columns (`put <key> <dx> <dy> [under] cols <a>-<b>`): K0 and
# K1 whole (the planted foot; the front toe tipped up at heel strike), K2 its ball end (cols 3-6 R: the heel-off), K3 its toe
# (2-5 on the ground, 4-5 lifted: fix r3, the walk pass's swing toe lifted 1 behind the planted heel at -6..-5, the run
# push's swing toe, the run contact's and flight's trailing toe, pointed, 2 rows up); the down frame's trailing toe at -3.
# Placed by `put` (pxc expands the stamps; `tags boots-stamped`).
# History (superseded for the side walk and run):
# Redrawn 2026-10-19 with the walk (std.pxm): both shoes show in every front and back frame (a step lifts one a row over
# the hem, never hides it); side views keep A3's flat tip (a 6 px shoe on a 7 px sole) with the planted sole centred on
# the plant anchor the man's legs use (round 2: one walk table for both bodies), a second shoe lifted behind the hem on
# the down frames, both off the ground in the run's flight; `stance` is A3's. Regions: B shoe, O sole (rags: bare feet).
use person woman
body adult
role legs tips
layer hangFront
anchor pivot
keys legs
z 9
stamps boots_adult
tags boots-stamped

